## Download

| Asset | Arch | SHA-256 |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ProtonDrive-CLI-{{VERSION}}-x86_64.AppImage` | x86_64 (Intel/AMD) | `{{SHA256_X86_64}}` |
| `ProtonDrive-CLI-{{VERSION}}-aarch64.AppImage` | aarch64 (ARM64) | `{{SHA256_AARCH64}}` |
| `SHA256SUMS` | checksums for both | — |

Verify: `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS`

## Run it

```bash
chmod +x ProtonDrive-CLI-{{VERSION}}-x86_64.AppImage
./ProtonDrive-CLI-{{VERSION}}-x86_64.AppImage --version
./ProtonDrive-CLI-{{VERSION}}-x86_64.AppImage --help
./ProtonDrive-CLI-{{VERSION}}-x86_64.AppImage auth login   # first run (opens your browser)
```

Put it on your `PATH` as `proton-drive`:

```bash
ln -s "$(pwd)/ProtonDrive-CLI-{{VERSION}}-x86_64.AppImage" ~/.local/bin/proton-drive
```

Both binaries need only **glibc ≥ 2.17**, so one file covers:

* **Arch / CachyOS** — works out of the box with `fuse2` installed
* **Debian / Ubuntu** — `sudo apt install libfuse2t64` (or `libfuse2` on older releases)
* **Fedora** — `sudo dnf install fuse-libs`

No FUSE (containers, restricted systems):
`APPIMAGE_EXTRACT_AND_RUN=1 ./ProtonDrive-CLI-{{VERSION}}-x86_64.AppImage --help`

Typical commands: `auth login`, `filesystem list /`, `filesystem upload <local> /`,
`filesystem download <remote> <dir>`, `sharing set-url …`, `photo timeline`,
`takeout run <dir>`. Full list: `--help`.

Desktop menu entry: install AppImageLauncher or run `appimaged` — the AppImage
ships a `Terminal=true` desktop file, 256/512 px icons and AppStream metadata.

## Integrity of the payload

`build.sh` downloads straight from `proton.me` and **aborts if the SHA-512 does
not match Proton's published checksum**:

* `linux-x64` → `{{SHA512_LINUX_X64}}`
* `linux-arm64` → `{{SHA512_LINUX_ARM64}}`

No Proton binary is committed to the repository — `download/`, `dist/`,
`tools/` and `build/` are git-ignored. The packaged bytes are identical to
Proton's downloads; nothing is patched, repacked or re-signed.

