## Build it yourself

```bash
git clone https://github.com/{{REPO}}.git
cd Proton-Drive-Linux-Cli
./scripts/check-upstream.sh   # sync with Proton's latest published version
./build.sh                    # both architectures
```

No `sudo` needed; `appimagetool` is downloaded automatically. Dependencies:
`wget`, `rsvg-convert` (librsvg), optionally `desktop-file-validate` and
`appstreamcli` for validation.

This repository checks Proton's download page automatically and publishes a new
release whenever upstream ships one — see "Automatic updates" in the README.
